Usage:
  x2c bootstrap --prefix <dir> [options]

Extract the source distribution carried by this APE and use the host
C compiler and archiver to install a native x2c under <dir>.

Output options:
      --prefix <dir>          Install native x2c and sources under <dir>

C compiler options:
      --cc <program>          Use <program> as the host C compiler
      --ar <program>          Use <program> as the static-library archiver
  -O0, -O1, -O2, -O3, -Os     Set C optimization

General options:
  -h, --help                  Show help and exit
  -v, --verbose               Show commands as they are executed
  -q, --quiet                 Suppress successful progress and receipts
      --plain                 Use stable output without terminal rendering
      --color <auto|always|never>
                              Control terminal color
  @<file>                     Read additional arguments from a response file

The seed supplies x2c sources and headers. A GCC- or Clang-compatible
C compiler and a compatible archiver must be installed.
